# # /snorql/
#
# Identifiers for Snorql-UI (https://github.com/wikipathways/Snorql-UI), the
# SPARQL query editor of the WikiPathways SPARQL endpoint, and for the format of
# the SPARQL example files it reads.
#
# https://w3id.org/snorql/ns
#   The vocabulary for SPARQL example files (terms such as
#   https://w3id.org/snorql/ns#alias). RDF clients asking for Turtle get the
#   Turtle file; everyone else gets the documentation of the example format.
#   https://w3id.org/snorql/ns.ttl always gives the Turtle file.
#
# https://w3id.org/snorql/param
#   Namespace for the names of example parameters
#   (https://w3id.org/snorql/param#species). It is not a vocabulary, so it
#   goes to the same documentation.
#
# https://w3id.org/snorql/
#   The Snorql-UI repository.
#
# ## Contact
# This space is administered by:
#
# Marvin Martens
# GitHub username: marvinm2

RewriteEngine on

RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} text/turtle
RewriteRule ^ns$ https://www.wikipathways.org/Snorql-UI/ns/snorql.ttl [R=303,L]
RewriteRule ^ns\.ttl$ https://www.wikipathways.org/Snorql-UI/ns/snorql.ttl [R=303,L]
RewriteRule ^(ns|param)$ https://github.com/wikipathways/Snorql-UI/blob/master/tools/examples/README.md [R=303,L]
RewriteRule ^$ https://github.com/wikipathways/Snorql-UI [R=302,L]
